Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:08:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11131/11362] [outer-loop] Score engines in the
 producer-evidence shape (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7020)

The producer evidence contract (exp6993, exp6994) moved an attempt from a flat
<game>/attempts/wm_*.py to a sealed <game>/attempts/evidence/<dir>/engine.py
carrying the engine with its transitions and envelope. The consumer did not
move with it.

The r11l eval emitted four engines and every one landed in the new shape, so
arc_induction_quality.py measured zero attempts from a run that produced four
and reported clean while doing it. A producer contract that ships without its
consumer leaves every future engine ungraded with every check green.

The path derivation needed widening as much as the glob. The new shape is two
levels deeper, so deriving the game from the parent directory files every
engine under the game 'evidence'. A dedicated mutation covers that.

Verified live against results/arc_e3: 61 models scored, 4 from evidence
directories, all filed under r11l as attempt at the expected byte counts.

Rejected: repointing DEFAULT_ROOT, which resolves to a job scratch directory
with a hardcoded session id. It is a real defect and it is recorded in the
spec, but changing it changes which population every past number was drawn
from, and the authorized change was to widen the shapes read.

Two test-suite-mutation markers were deleted deliberately, per the guard's own
'if the rewrite is intended' instruction. Both named exactly one path,
scripts/arc_induction_quality.py, both recorded attributed_to_run: [] and
detected it at 02:04:43Z and 02:04:44Z, which is when I was editing that file.
The conductor's pytest run did not write it; the guard saw an authored edit
inside a concurrent test window and could not tell whose it was. Nothing else
was protected by either marker, and neither was reverted.

6 tests, 3/3 mutations RED with byte-identical restores.

